{"availability":"available","full":"cpeoples/cudabom","name":"cudabom","description":"🧊 Evidence-backed CUDA bill of materials: identifies CUDA components in binaries, archives, and container images, generates security-grade SBOM/VEX (CycloneDX), and matches known NVIDIA advisories. SLSA Build Level 3, Sigstore-signed.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-30T07:37:02Z","updated":"2026-10-16T12:03:19Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cpeoples.github.io/cudabom/","topics":["advisories","binary-analysis","cli","cuda","cyclonedx","devsecops","elf","gpu","nvidia","rust","sbom","security","security-scanner","security-tools","sigstore","slsa","software-composition-analysis","supply-chain-security","vex","vulnerability-scanner"],"demo":"https://cpeoples.github.io/cudabom/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T13:22:12.200Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T13:22:12.200Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T13:22:12.200Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:06:14.641Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T13:22:12.200Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["cudabom is an open-source Rust CLI that proves which NVIDIA CUDA software is actually inside an artifact (Python wheels, shared libraries, executables, and container images) and turns that evidence into security-grade SBOM, advisory, and VEX data.","What CUDA is really inside this artifact, how do we know, and are we affected by any NVIDIA security bulletin?","Deliberate scope, not a missing feature. cudabom's thesis is evidence over declaration: what you write (source) and declare (manifests) routinely disagrees with what actually lands in the shipped binary. Source says intent; the artifact tells the truth."],"features":["-lcublas in a build, or import torch in a .py, tells you something was","Source and lockfile analysis is also environment-dependent (toolchain, flags,"